issue_comments.body:
Thanks @stecasta — all four minors addressed in 07845a0:
- description now says two declaration sites (indexer + FlashInfer sparse);
- the settled `[64, 128]` note in the test is trimmed to a one-line comment;
- added `test_sm12x_default_launch_resolves_64_for_full_set`, which resolves the default through `Platform._preferred_block_size_for_backends` over the full DSv4.1 set (indexer, FlashInfer sparse, sparse SWA, compressor) and asserts 64 — the quantity the PR actually changes;
- the non-SM12x check is parametrized over SM90 (`[64]`) and SM100 (`[128]`).

Landing order stays as agreed: after #60948, or together with the #57292 guard.

@xzwgit @Lei-010 one cell for the IPC × DSpark isolation, on 0.32.0 + this PR (FlashInfer 0.7.2.post1, 8× RTX PRO 6000 Server Edition, TP8), using Lei-010's 3-layer probe:

- **IPC off + DSpark k=7 flat, probabilistic/block → CLEAN** (0 fails across determinism ×20, 512-token degeneration, concurrency 8/16/32). IPC off + k=3 also clean. So the corruption needs the IPC path, not DSpark alone.
- **IPC on doesn't boot on AWS g7e.48xlarge** (`CUDART error: peer access is not supported between these two devices` in `pcie_ipc_ar` init): GPU P2P there is only available within PCIe-switch pairs, so the IPC × DSpark failure can't occur on that topology.

@Lei-010 The quadrant plan looks right, and your arm-matching discipline is better than what we'd have asked for. Two notes from our side:

1. **Row 6 at capture 512 with the caveat flagged is fine — don't spend the extra restart.** On the failing stack we already cleared the capture axis independently (our six-leg isolation included a capture-size arm that stayed corrupted identically), so capture 512 vs 1024 is not load-bearing for interpretation on this stack. If row 6 comes back corrupted, runner flavour is the last axis standing and row 7 is optional color rather than a needed control.
2. For row 5 vs our row 4, the only deltas should be k (3 flat vs 7 flat+probabilistic) — same V1, same capture 1024. If row 5 is clean, the suspicion narrows to the k=7 draft chain length × IPC interaction, which would also explain why your production (k3-scheduled) never tripped.
